  "notes": "Cash basis audit. Governmental lines from the governmental funds statement of receipts, disbursements and changes in fund balances (p4, Total column); interest income printed under Other Financing Sources below the total is a receipt marked outside_printed_total. Business-type from the proprietary funds statement (p6, Total column): interest income, capital outlay and debt service under Other Receipts (Disbursements) marked outside_printed_total. Business-type ending cash 368,072 includes restricted customer-deposit cash 10,726. Balance sheet from the government-wide Statement of Net Position - Cash Basis (p1, Total column), since the governmental funds statement (p3) differs in restricted/unassigned split and the proprietary side carries customer deposits. Detail: the only supplementary schedules are an all-funds combined budget-and-actual schedule (p11), a total-only comparative governmental statement (p9) and a proprietary comparative statement (p10) that disagrees with p6 for the Water fund; per the per-fund detail rule, detail is one line per fund column of the governmental (p4) and proprietary (p6) statements; the combined budget schedule lines are not recorded. Sanitation fund expenditures and charges for services are inside the General Fund column. Read pages 1-11 of 11."
